Subject: [PATCH] wifi: iwlwifi: bind 0xA840 (BE201) with any subsystem ID

Lunar Lake CNVi (8086:A840, Intel BE201) is listed only with a fixed set
of subsystem IDs. Laptops with an ID missing from that list, such as the
Samsung Galaxy Book 5, get no driver at all: no wlan interface and no
log message. For Bz devices the configuration comes from the RF detected
at probe time (iwl_dev_info_table, RF_TYPE(FM)), not from the subsystem
ID, exactly as for 0x7740 and 0x4D40 that already match PCI_ANY_ID.

Add a PCI_ANY_ID entry after the explicit ones.

Upstream: Not submitted (local correction)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/pcie/drv.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/pcie/drv.c
@@ -539,6 +539,8 @@
 	{IWL_PCI_DEVICE(0xA840, 0x1776, iwl_bz_mac_cfg)},
 	{IWL_PCI_DEVICE(0xA840, 0x1735, iwl_bz_mac_cfg)},
 	{IWL_PCI_DEVICE(0xA840, 0x1736, iwl_bz_mac_cfg)},
+	/* Sweetspot: any subsystem ID, the RF is detected like 0x7740 */
+	{IWL_PCI_DEVICE(0xA840, PCI_ANY_ID, iwl_bz_mac_cfg)},
 	{IWL_PCI_DEVICE(0x7740, PCI_ANY_ID, iwl_bz_mac_cfg)},
 	{IWL_PCI_DEVICE(0x4D40, PCI_ANY_ID, iwl_bz_mac_cfg)},

